            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="0607" n="603" xml:id="pg603"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/793: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-03T19:00:00+09:00">June 3, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 3—7:13 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>352. Our 332, May 26, 8 p.m. It was announced this afternoon that General Itagaki
                    is appointed Minister of War vice General Sugiyama, resigned.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai for Hankow and Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
